sentences.l:
for even if in his heart he is minded to make war,
yet unseen his limbs grow heavy, and thirst comes upon him
and hunger, and his knees are hampered as he goes.

choosing out young men, the best men of all the Achaeans,
to bring the gifts from beside my ship, as many as to Achilles
yesterday we promised to give, and to lead the women;

but now those lie mangled, whom
Hector, Priam’s-son, subdued, when Zeus gave him glory,
and you two urge to food;
